       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "ocean",
       "kind": "point",
       "text": "But they live underwater"
      },
      {
       "at_word": "how",
       "kind": "title",
       "text": "How do they sleep?"
      }
     ]
    },
    "phu_de": "Here's a puzzle. | Dolphins are mammals, | so they need air to breathe. | But they live in the ocean. | So how do they sleep | without drowning?"
   },
   "voice": {
    "t0": 0.1,
    "dur": 9.024,
    "file": "build/audio/hook.wav"
   },
   "text": "Here's a puzzle. Dolphins are mammals, so they need air to breathe. But they live in the ocean. So how do they sleep without drowning?",
   "t1": 9.374
  },
  {
   "id": "problem",
   "t0": 9.374,
   "data": {
    "huashu": {
     "grammar": "y3_whiteboard",
     "cues": [
      {
       "at_word": "breathe",
       "kind": "draw",
       "text": "You breathe on autopilot",
       "data": {
        "icon": "person"
       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "every",
       "kind": "point",
       "text": "Dolphins decide every breath"
      },
      {
       "at_word": "fall",
       "kind": "draw",
       "text": "Fully asleep = stop breathing",
       "data": {
        "icon": "cross"
       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "breathing",
       "kind": "highlight",
       "data": {
        "target": "draw",
        "index": 1
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    "phu_de": "Humans breathe automatically. | You never have to think | about it. | A dolphin's breath is voluntary. | Every single breath | is a conscious decision. | Fall completely asleep, | and a dolphin | would stop breathing."
   },
   "voice": {
    "t0": 9.524,
    "dur": 13.8,
    "file": "build/audio/problem.wav"
   },
   "text": "Humans breathe automatically. You never have to think about it. A dolphin's breath is voluntary. Every single breath is a conscious decision. Fall completely asleep, and a dolphin would stop breathing.",
   "t1": 23.574
  },
  {
   "id": "trick",
   "t0": 23.574,
   "data": {
    "huashu": {
     "grammar": "y3_whiteboard",
     "cues": [
      {
       "at_word": "half",
       "kind": "draw",
       "text": "Half the brain sleeps",
       "data": {
        "icon": "network"
       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "other",
       "kind": "point",
       "text": "One half at a time"
      },
      {
       "at_word": "unihemispheric",
       "kind": "point",
       "text": "Unihemispheric slow-wave sleep"
      },
      {
       "at_word": "sleep",
       "nth": 2,
       "kind": "highlight",
       "data": {
        "target": "point",
        "index": 1
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    "phu_de": "So dolphins evolved | a clever workaround. | They sleep with only half | of their brain at a time. | The other half stays awake. | Scientists call it | unihemispheric slow-wave sleep."
   },
   "voice": {
    "t0": 23.724,
    "dur": 12.0,
    "file": "build/audio/trick.wav"
   },
   "text": "So dolphins evolved a clever workaround. They sleep with only half of their brain at a time. The other half stays awake. Scientists call it unihemispheric slow-wave sleep.",
   "t1": 35.974
  },
  {
   "id": "eye",
   "t0": 35.974,
   "data": {
    "huashu": {
     "grammar": "y3_whiteboard",
     "cues": [
      {
       "at_word": "duty",
       "kind": "draw",
       "text": "Awake half on duty",
       "data": {
        "icon": "target"
       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "open",
       "kind": "draw",
       "text": "One eye open",
       "data": {
        "icon": "person"
       }
      },
      {
       "at_word": "opposite",
       "kind": "point",
       "text": "Eye opposite the sleeping half"
      },
      {
       "at_word": "predators",
       "kind": "highlight",
       "data": {
        "target": "draw",
        "index": 1
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    "phu_de": "The sleeping half rests, | while the awake half | stays on duty. | And here is the giveaway. | A sleeping dolphin | keeps one eye open. | The eye on the opposite side | of the sleeping half, | watching for predators."
   },
   "voice": {
    "t0": 36.124,
    "dur": 13.464,
    "file": "build/audio/eye.wav"
   },
   "text": "The sleeping half rests, while the awake half stays on duty. And here is the giveaway. A sleeping dolphin keeps one eye open. The eye on the opposite side of the sleeping half, watching for predators.",
   "t1": 49.838
  },
  {
   "id": "resting",
   "t0": 49.838,
   "data": {
    "huashu": {
     "grammar": "y3_whiteboard",
     "cues": [
      {
       "at_word": "drift",
